<chapter xml:id="probability-uncertainty">
  <title>Probability and Uncertainty</title>
  <section xml:id="probability-randomness">
    <title>Data varies</title>
    <p>Statistical analysis treats variation as information rather than inconvenience. Probability models describe uncertainty and give us a language for distinguishing signal from noise.</p>
  </section>
  <section xml:id="probability-inference">
    <title>From a sample to a wider claim</title>
    <p>Confidence intervals, standard errors, and hypothesis tests all depend on assumptions about how the data were generated. Their output should be interpreted with those assumptions visible.</p>
  </section>
</chapter>
